CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function-scoped labels: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [stmt.label]/1: label scope is the function; the same label name in
two functions was a spurious "duplicate label" (the defined-labels map
was not reset per function body in the C++ front end, unlike the C one).
Found by dog-fooding big-int/bigint.cc.  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.
